// TC-CA-9: invariantNotEstablished suppresses both the loop body deadBranch
// and the post-loop deadBranch.
//
// loop_invariant false can never be established — Silicon adds assume false
// after the failed assertion, making the loop body unreachable as a cascade.
// postLoopSuppressor = () => invNotEstablishedFired suppresses both.
//
// Expected errors: 1 (invariantNotEstablished only).
// Body deadBranch: SUPPRESSED (cascade from invariantNotEstablished).
// Post-loop deadBranch: SUPPRESSED (same suppressor).
void f(int x) {
    loop_invariant false;
    while (x > 0) {
        x = x - 1; // body deadBranch suppressed — cascade artifact
    }
}
